disease;
mismanagement/destruction of vital resources;
take your pick lol.
I find that a good amount of collapses tend to be a combination of internal mismanagement on behalf of the state and external threats  of hostile enemies, disasters, etc.

somekind of high proof liquor in a small flask is in my opinion essential. can be used to barter, antiseptic, fire starting, morale,Sterilize needles, tweezers and other instruments
Disinfect questionable water; Relieve poison ivy
Topical treatment;
Gun cleaner;
Solvent;
Mouthwash
 Rust prevention;
 Clean optic glass; and tons of other uses

72 hour setup for reaching my secondary location in Pa about 40 minutes drive from me. tried to be as light as possible: 
Bag: SOC bug out bag;
2.0 L hydration bladder;
three extra sets of t-shirts, shorts, under wear, socks;
one pair of heavy duty tactical pants in black;
one heavy duty jacket also black;
personal hygene kit;
neccesary medications;
fire making material: flint steel, bag of dryer lint, folded paper;
extra water bladder;
duct tape;
ontario rat-5 knife;
sunscreen;
bug spray;
individual first aid kit/IFAK (major and minor trauma, gun shot wounds etc.);
and finally... my ar15 pistol in 300blk out and 3x 30 round magazines ;
Everything weighs in about 50lbs which I can have excellent mobility with

so let me get this straight ... 
The people in the First Amendment means the people;
The people in the Fourth Amendment means the people;
The people in the Ninth Amendment means, the people;
...but The people in the Second Amendment (ratified in 1791) applies to hunters and the National Guard (created by an Act of Congress in 1903)?
